# @tribal: OTEL FOCUS = FinOps Open Cost and Usage Specification. b00t uses FOCUS
# log stream semantics for command-level cost attribution (tokens, time, tier).
# 🤓: BFO_0000040 = Material Entity — the OTEL server IS a physical process resource.

## Problem

# b00t executes hundreds of commands per session but has no quantified signal on:
# - Which commands are run most (recipe optimization target)
# - Which guards fire most (guard tuning signal → self-improve loop)
# - Which datum types are unknown (type system evolution signal)
# - Token cost per command tier (sm0l/ch0nky/frontier budget attribution)
#
# Without metrics, the self-improve loop (PRD-ARCH-004) is blind.
# Without OTEL, b00t can't integrate with operator's existing observability stack.

## Finished State

# `b00t session status --metrics` prints current session OTEL summary:
# ```
# Session 630696 | 07:00-08:30 | 52 cmds | 14 guard hits | 3 unknown types
# Top commands: b00t datum filter (12), cargo check (8), b00t task list (5)
# Guard hits: pip_guard(0) find_guard(3) force_push_guard(0)
# Token tiers: sm0l 12k | ch0nky 48k | frontier 210k
# ```
#
# `b00t session otel --scrape` emits Prometheus text format for external scraper.
#
# `b00t session otel --focus` emits OTEL FOCUS JSON log stream to stdout/file.

## Architecture

# b00t-otel crate (new, minimal): embedded metrics server.
# Uses opentelemetry-sdk + opentelemetry-prometheus (already MIT-licensed).
# Metrics are session-scoped (reset on new session); exported on demand.
#
# ```
# [session state]
#     ↓ instrument
# [b00t-otel]  ←── OtelCollector::record(event: MetricEvent)
#     ↓ on demand
# [/metrics scrape]  OR  [FOCUS JSON stream]  OR  [guard-violations.jsonl append]
# ```
#
# MetricEvent variants:
# - CommandRun { cmd: String, tier: Tier, duration_ms: u64, tokens: Option<u64> }
# - GuardHit { guard_name: String, action: GuardAction, cmd: String }
# - DatumTypeUnknown { type_str: String }
# - DatumFilterRun { type_tag: Option<String>, result_count: usize }
# - TaskUpdate { task_id: u32, status: String }

## FOCUS Log Stream

# FinOps Open Cost and Usage Spec (FOCUS) fields for b00t command events:
#
# | FOCUS field    | b00t mapping                          |
# |----------------|---------------------------------------|
# | BilledCost     | token_count * tier_cost_per_token     |
# | ResourceType   | tier (sm0l / ch0nky / frontier)       |
# | ServiceName    | "b00t"                                |
# | ResourceId     | session_pid                           |
# | Tags/cmd       | command string (truncated to 64 chars)|
# | UsageAmount    | token_count                           |
# | UsageUnit      | "tokens"                              |
#
# Stream target: `B00T_OTEL_FOCUS_FILE` env var (default: `guard-violations.jsonl` sidecar)
# OR `B00T_OTEL_ENDPOINT` for OTLP gRPC push.

## Known Recipes (Counter-Backed)

# Each guard entry gains a `hit_count: AtomicU64` field populated at runtime.
# Each `[[b00t.hive.guards]]` entry gets a `recipe_id` derived from pattern hash.
# The OTEL server exposes:
#   b00t_guard_hits_total{guard="find_guard", action="warn"} 3
#   b00t_command_runs_total{cmd="cargo check"} 8
#   b00t_unknown_datum_types_total{type="prd"} 1

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `b00t-otel` crate: `OtelCollector::new()`, `record(MetricEvent)`, `scrape() -> String`
# - [ ] Guard eval path instruments GuardHit on every fire
# - [ ] `deserialize_datum_type` instruments DatumTypeUnknown (already warns; add metric)
# - [ ] `b00t session status --metrics` prints session summary
# - [ ] `b00t session otel --scrape` emits valid Prometheus text
# - [ ] `b00t session otel --focus` emits valid OTEL FOCUS JSON
# - [ ] `B00T_OTEL_ENDPOINT` env → OTLP gRPC push (optional, guarded by feature flag)
# - [ ] Test: inject 3 GuardHit events → scrape shows count=3

